[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2596855202","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101633#issuecomment-2596855202","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101633","id":2596855202,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ayN2i","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-16T20:45:06Z","updated_at":"2025-01-16T22:51:56Z","body":"I don't see much point in adding overall gravity, as it is sufficient to direct the external force in the same direction as the gravity.\r\n\r\nAlso, I don't think gravity override is very useful. Since the direction of gravity is different for each joint, overriding it will result in forces in a direction not intended by the designer.\r\n\r\nIt possibly makes sense to add options such as use_world_gravity_dir and relative_from_world_gravity_dir, but then we need to think about the conversion of the rotation in direction when a particular joint wants to point gravity sideways.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.git